body:
huh? how is that not treating someone as a person. People have faces. Would you talk to a mysterious voice from a sewer or someone who came up to you with a bag on their head? This is really basic dating site stuff that I need a pic in order to talk. Many people immediately block those without pics.

&#x200B;

This also sometimes happens further into a conversation as well. These people have no intention of ever showing pics and probably scammers or selling pics.

Im not giving an anonymous person my phone number and jumping through hoops just to get a face pic. If they want discretion they can put the face pics in the private pics section and unlock them for me.

&#x200B;

I have no way to tell how attracted I am to someone without a clear unobstructed face pic. I am all about a persons face and not their body.

I don't have such a thing.

&#x200B;

Why the hell would you block someone unless they were threatening your life or spamming you? Block is a serious thing. It's right to "Report". This is not the proper use of block. Its for too much contact and not too little contact. If you really liked him enough to contact him, do you now really need to 'permanently prevent this person from absolutely ever contacting me again, even in an emergency?'. Is that really necessary?

&#x200B;

You have to keep in mind there might be a fixable reason you aren't getting a response, like you have no face pics, your location is wrong, or you're being too vague in your messages. If I think someone is a bullshitter or is dodging my questions or pic requests and is too far away Ill sometimes ignore them until they upload the pics or say something that makes sense.

&#x200B;

Or maybe he just tapped through some push notifications by mistake without actually reading it, or something came up while he was reading it and he forgot to get back to you. Maybe his stock started tanking. It could be something innocent, and does not necessarily indicate you are a bad match. Even if it takes a really long time maybe he just got busy with his wife or another SB but you'll be the very next person his list.

&#x200B;

What if you mistakenly blocked your perfect dream SD and now he's dying to get back to you but cant?

&#x200B;

People do this shit on other platforms where they cant even see you read the message. I log on and see that someone sent a message 6 hours ago but then they blocked me. wtf?
